.TH GECKO-DESKTOP 1 "October 2026" "gecko" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gecko-desktop \- native window for the Gecko terminal multiplexer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gecko-desktop
[\fB\-\-url=\fIurl\fR] [\fB\-\-size=\fIW,H\fR] [\fB\-\-position=\fIX,Y\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A see-through window around Gecko's web UI. \fBgecko open\fR starts it with
the daemon's URL. Without \fB\-\-url\fR it finds this user's running Gecko
daemon, or starts one, and opens it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GECKO_HOME
Gecko's directory (default \fI~/.gecko-terminal\fR).
.TP
.B GECKO_DESKTOP_NO_SANDBOX=1
Run without Chromium's sandbox, for systems where it can't start.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gecko (1)
